Item 4 concerns advertising. The firm's quarterly performance summary prese=
nts a composite return for the balanced strategy that excludes three accoun=
ts closed during the periods shown. The staff's recalculation including tho=
se accounts produces a return between 40 and 110 basis points lower in each=
 of the eight quarters tested. The summary carries no disclosure of the exc=
lusion, no statement of whether returns are net or gross of advisory fees, =
and no description of the composite's construction. The staff regards a pre=
sentation of this kind as misleading within the meaning of Rule 206(4)-1(a)=
(5).<br />
<br />
The firm should not distribute the summary in its present form. If it inten=
ds to continue publishing composite performance, the response should descri=
be how the composite will be constructed, who will verify it, and what disc=
losure will accompany it.<br />
<br />
The remaining four items are described in the letter and are not related to=
 Item 4.<br />
